.THS Active 5L News.SH NAMEActive - List of existing newsgroups with indicies..SH DESCRIPTION.ti +3This file contains a list of all existing newsgroup on the localinstallation. The file is in general managed via.B controlmessagesbut for some reasons you may edit it. It.I mustbe sorted to ensure that news works properly. the format is in general.ce<group> <last> <first> n<flag> [<sizelimit>]for non moderated groups,.ce<group> <last> <first> y<flag> [<sizelimit>] [<moderator(s)>]for moderated groups and.ce<group> <last> <first> r<flag> [<sizelimit>]for read-only groups where.B <group>is the name of the newsgroup in lowercase letters,.B <first>is the first (oldest) avaiable article and.B <last>is the last <newest> avaiable article. The newsarticel are stored with afilename of a number. The.B <flag>may be either.B uor.B ito tell that this newsgroup is \fBu\fBsed or \fBi\fBgnored.  If a groupis moderated then the moderator(s) should be inserted after the.B yflag with their full mail address.If there is a number after the flags only articles with less or equal insize of kBytes will be stored.